# K03 RECEIVE-OUTPUT (Codex K03-RECEIVE-OUTPUT-20261007-23; LMX_blog/q/q53.md:95-97; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# #construction, #dynamic): a computed output -- a receiver's, merge's, a computed number declaration's -- at a named
# Structure's top level is no field of it, stored at its own receiver occurrence, produced when control reaches it.
# `receiveMessage: m MainLetter` at Host's top level: C main posts one letter; nothing is taken before Host runs,
# Host's run takes it (m, its sender, its payload's arguments), and the same written occurrence on the second run takes
# the empty inbox's 0.  @m is not read here (unit_output_named_receive_address, Codex -24).  Exit 7; 80 if Host's body
# ran before its call, 81 if the first run did not take the letter, 82 if the second run did not reuse the occurrence.
MainLetter:
    char: []: []: mainArgs
end: MainLetter
Out:
    int: runs 0
    int: got 0
    int: bad 0
end: Out
Host:
    receiveMessage: m MainLetter
    Out\runs: Out\runs + 1
    if: m != 0
        Out\got: Out\got + 1
        if: m\sender = 0
            Out\bad: 1
        if: length(m\payload\mainArgs) = 0
            Out\bad: 1
end: Host
fn: probe () int
    if: Out\runs != 0
        return: 80
    Host()
    if: Out\runs != 1 || Out\got != 1 || Out\bad != 0
        return: 81
    Host()
    if: Out\runs != 2 || Out\got != 1 || Out\bad != 0
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: probe
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: probe(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
